Cadence demo CPU adapter

backend/cpu_runtime.py is an unchanged copy of the coordinated Cadence CPU
qualification artifact generalization_cpu_v1/cpu_runtime.py. Its module declares
new wrapper contributions under Apache-2.0. Source SHA256:
9f64f137a55f553428bbf3dfff1e4a5127b1a24506d7208a6057e67e753a93fe

This demo exposes only the FP32 profile at four threads. The adapter reconstructs
the pinned public BF16-rounded merged Kev base before promoting the model to
FP32. It is a separate precision profile from the public CUDA runtime.

Cadence, Kev and Qwen upstream code/model authorship and licenses remain in the
pinned public package's LICENSE, LICENSE.QWEN, NOTICE and NOTICE.QWEN. This demo
does not bundle their model weights or dataset rows. No upstream endorsement or
CUDA/CPU numerical equivalence is implied.
